= The Party Is Broken

The district offices are closed. Their secretaries are in prison, abroad or dead, and the membership lists have been seized or burned. Fewer than a thousand people in Germany still pay their dues, and most of them do not know who to pay them to.

The few who are left meet in each other's kitchens and talk about the old days.

- @end: See how it ends.

